CMPT 276 Project - Phase 1, Use Cases
Group 25

Primary Actor: User/Player

Scenario:
1.	The “Start” screen is displayed to User
2.	User presses the play button
3.	User will read instructions
4.	User presses “Start” button to start playing game
5.	The system displays the maze with User’s character as a car
6.	The timer will start to count down by 1 second
7.	The progression/points bar will start empty
8.	User will press UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT key to move the main character (car)
9.	The User moves the main character to collect coins (coin disappears from cell after being caught) to earn points 
10.	User will avoid being caught by the Concord officer by moving UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT using the corresponding keys on keyboard
11.	The User collects a student’s wallet and will gain more points for progression bar (mischief points), the student’s wallet will disappear from cell
12.	The User collects enough points to fill up the progression bar before the timer ends 
13.	The User moves the main character to reach the exit/ticket booth
14.	The “You Win” screen is displayed to the User showing the final score and time
15.	User presses the “Play Again” button to play again

Exceptions:
1.	User Presses the “Quit” button to quit playing the game – “Start” screen (beginning screen) should be displayed to User
2.	User tries to move the main character into a wall – main character should not be able to move into a wall, and will remain in its current cell
3.	User tries to move the main character into a traffic cone– main character should not be able to move into the traffic cone, and will remain in its current cell
4.	User is caught by the Concord officer – “Game Over” screen should be displayed with the option for User to either play again or quit playing by pressing the corresponding buttons
5.	User moves main character into an idling car – progression bar should lose a few points
6.	User does not collect the student’s wallet in time and the student’s wallet disappears – progression bar remains the same but User will not gain any bonus points
7.	User does not collect enough points before the timer runs out – “Game Over” screen is displayed with the option for User to either play again or quit playing
8.	User collected enough points but did not reach the exit/ticket booth before the timer ran out – “Game Over” screen is displayed with the option for User to either play again or quit playing by pressing the corresponding buttons
9.	Concord officer runs into an idling car, coin, or student’s wallet – the reward/punishment is not affected and remains on its cell
10.	Concord officer tries to move into the wall of parked cars or the traffic cones – Concord officer remains in its current cell
11.	User loses enough points such that the progression bar has a negative value (negative amount of points) – “Game Over” screen is displayed with the option for User to either play again or quit playing by pressing the corresponding buttons
12.	User does not press a button on keyboard (or does not press a valid button on keyboard) – main character will not move

